<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A few weeks ago, Alessio Dionisi was force=
d to deny the =E2=80=9Cfake news=E2=80=9D he had joined Sean Dyche, Gianfra=
nco Zola, Beppe Sannino, =C3=93scar Garc=C3=ADa, Billy McKinlay, Slavisa Jo=
kanovic, Quique S=C3=A1nchez Flores (twice), Walter Mazzarri, Marco Silva, =
Javi Gracia (twice), Nigel Pearson, Vladimir Ivic, Xisco Mu=C3=B1oz, Claudi=
o Ranieri, Roy Hodgson, Rob Edwards, Slaven Bilic, Chris Wilder, Val=C3=A9r=
ien Ismael, Tom Cleverley, Paulo Pezzolano and Edward Still in being sacked=
 by the Pozzo family since 2012. There was no denial on Sunday, when the ax=
e inevitably fell on the head coach following a 4-0 shellacking at Sheffiel=
d United and the Italian left after only 18 games in charge. While his reig=
n is unlikely to live long in the memory of anyone at Vicarage Road, Dionis=
i can at least boast on his LinkedIn page that in terms of longevity under =
the Pozzos, he took charge of 18 more matches than Dyche, 17 more than Garc=
=C3=ADa and 16 more than McKinlay. Indeed, he even outlasted Rob Edwards, w=
ho was assured he would be backed =E2=80=9Ccome hell or high water=E2=80=9D=
 upon his 2022 appointment, only to be fired from the ejector seat 11 games=
 later.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s been quite the white-knuckle =
ride for Watford since the Pozzos arrived, armed only with a spreadsheet, a=
n army of Udinese cast-offs and knowledge of the loophole that there was no=
 Football League cap on the number of players who could be brought in on lo=
an from clubs outside the UK. And while few fans will be able to recall all=
 25 of the coaches who have been hired and fired by the Pozzos, they do hav=
e fond memories to take to the grave. There was that <a href=3D"https://abl=
ink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgsz=
cCSneHECQaBbvLJ3KB3GLdzUuTigSIqnoQ_bCAi1AGBY3oN0ld3rrIr6J-iiyoJNt3JtNz3Ovy6=
yOtwDCRWDBF3wvtsFVN0YQi-MbTafzku9Jt7GjlClnqV5LUBCwARUHema0ox8jF3_OtBKjmVmZv=
Fy3d3gBoU6lC-whCGenxLOoJ0q9ezqOJurawed1QR_Kzwju57dg70ch89JNIPgVst7BABzH5Te4=
C2hHmjZ1RUmjT--HUk9ylgkCTb770jtERU2CMxnJsPDrf3ZtrRXIeNe2qMzn64G3XQRClDfYy5D=
R_EuAGZL0YnXIcvFTC83BRQWU0cY/4w3/xFvIhKc1R9apfwz5SoVeYA/h28/h001.u8UB1bkIue=
2DBYEk57EaotXGQD1yMbtkc7KcCyx_kWA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">end-to-end Tro=
y Deeney play-off semi-final goal</a> against Leicester. There were five un=
interrupted seasons in the Premier League. There was that time they ended L=
iverpool=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c=
/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECQaBbvLJ3KB3GLdzUuTigSKaLw3=
8zkP-t0bNT9VCNr3SMtnLbW5MfwuR-NBM3TKSuGdlngUTU3vB78Puqz29p9cdd8dparsxyRYW3M=
tCSomlPwFTX-DRCmvxvadr1zaTmoHgx_VLBxvK0XJ1_NXVhdmFGEk6miv6XX0p6sZ8Lv1zBQmfX=
wNqgOMt9IK1_9p3nNV8hY3DrvAxdA3HWIVqTZZnNFQysEiyiOJyE5VQ2ZpfdxllaflrXe5c8Qq1=
RpCvs/4w3/xFvIhKc1R9apfwz5SoVeYA/h29/h001.XQestlXPepLpBue59Sc9IZ1K0KjTrhIvS=
_AQuYRVArc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">44-match unbeaten Premier League run<=
/a> despite being stuck in the relegation zone. And what self-respecting Ho=
rnet will ever forget travelling to watch their team play in the <a href=3D=
"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyT=
NtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECzMA3M_vNoZYMbp2QFaK37-I93kQgPoLO_rmVBNpiAJ5c1EOvxesFCp4=
niYsGw7z6Py794BHDgEbbxM86BIExc-tPXsXu75NWkob19eNfhBuyoWsrTGuRgh_sdsL67AGMgq=
AwgIHXHX0RF8OJd_8NMX-zbHTx5rP-v6KGwF0rcBgZFIKSdbeZBHBWzRZF88emudohyk9sn79C8=
BOHtxO77RJ5E2bklYThZULayB30nZZRqRKacv4IS_k4dWMN7hLaBtco49ozF_DzJxL-E0SNN/4w=
3/xFvIhKc1R9apfwz5SoVeYA/h30/h001.9LzCPpsavr3E7gksyijFvFsCMks9e3krWp_sJcdS5=
7Q" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">2019 FA Cup final</a>?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Of course it hasn=E2=80=99t all been rosy =
in the Pozzo garden. The eight-day managerial reign of McKinlay was a sourc=
e of much mirth for fans of rival clubs. A double relegation from the Premi=
er League =E2=80=93 the first amid allegations of a dressing-room bust-up l=
inked to <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_J=
kLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECQaBbvLJ3KB3GLdzUuTigSOZcXjOMHscFtu8g=
4rgAsRvv_HVXyUbOXZXqPB5jJmGL7KZR48gAMxcYMIgrEHPOeadtYQ7bczYtN9vTjik7TsfpKWS=
6TKhvNZEo8bkJtgcnoL8IDYQj-n2HyBAk6NSziVOwEkeJAhAnqcCpzlRLiGBArZACF_s8EyB1e3=
eh-tgZOflTx6_dIMoOUtz1qHnWErV6rc-Tsjs4tTl28rN40hBKgcwnYKx_HvHlI94Hyqf0/4w3/=
xFvIhKc1R9apfwz5SoVeYA/h31/h001.XzOxGAFEvWl-TM78KunNXm0cLFd1WeqyEW-7VwnqDok=
" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">an illegal lockdown party</a> =E2=80=93 wasn=E2=
=80=99t great either. Playing I=E2=80=99m Still Standing by Elton John, the=
 club=E2=80=99s honorary life president, over the Vicarage Road PA system t=
o mark their descent into the Championship heaped further embarrassment upo=
n the club. And what self-respecting Hornet will ever forget travelling hom=
e after watching their team play in the <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial=
.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECzMA3M=
_vNoZYMbp2QFaK37-I93kQgPoLO_rmVBNpiAJ5c1EOvxesFCp4niYsGw7z6Py794BHDgEbbxM86=
BIExc-tPXsXu75NWkob19eNfhBuyoWsrTGuRgh_sdsL67AGMgqAwgIHXHX0RF8OJd_8NMX-zbHT=
x5rP-v6KGwF0rcBgZFIKSdbeZBHBWzRZF88emudohyk9sn79C8BOHtxO77RJ5E2bklYThZULayB=
30nZZRqRKacv4IS_k4dWMN7hLaBtco49ozF_DzJxL-E0SNN/4w3/xFvIhKc1R9apfwz5SoVeYA/=
h32/h001.-2o5WIBT3ZjPvFxZb73OpU-7Te1XYI_8UqLmuNlMA-0" style=3D"color: #0077=
B6;">2019 FA Cup final</a>?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">While it would be foolish to predict what =
will happen next at a club that currently sit two places above the Champion=
ship relegation zone, the one stonewall certainty is that the name =E2=80=
=9CEdward Iordanescu=E2=80=9D will be the next to be copied and pasted into=
 the over-worked club template announcing a managerial departure. The Roman=
ian was formally introduced this morning and with this being his 14th job i=
n the past 16 years, he can arguably lay claim to being the most =E2=80=98W=
atford=E2=80=99 manager of the Pozzo era. =E2=80=9CFor me, I want a team th=
at plays very good, organised football with the spirit and attitude, and th=
e strong mentality,=E2=80=9D he blathered, as local reporters dabbed their =
bingo cards. =E2=80=9CAnd then, yes, regarding the organisation of the team=
, that takes time.=E2=80=9D History suggests getting the time he needs is a=
 pipe dream for Iordanescu, whose first game in charge is away at Champions=
hip basement-dwellers Derby County. Should Watford go to Pride Park and los=
e, he could be out of a job by Saturday night.</p>
